<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 18:59:19 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>Washington set to approve $2.8 bn arms package for Israel</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/washington-set-to-approve-2-8-bn-arms-package-for-israel</link><description>
The US federal government is on track to approve a $2.8 billion arms package for Israel, US media reported Tuesday, with the sale of 40,000 one-ton bombs among the largest munitions packages sold in recent years. The Washington Post said the package -- funded with US taxpayer dollars -- featured some of the most destructive munitions in Western arsenals, including 20,000 MK-84s, 20,000 BLU-117s, and 20,000 I-2000 Penetrator warheads. FRANCE 24's Selina Sykes reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/942153e2-b1fb-11f1-bd55-3df65e1cd14d/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-17306261656aaade6612d4f8-79538850.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/942153e2-b1fb-11f1-bd55-3df65e1cd14d/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-17306261656aaade6612d4f8-79538850.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2e26b3bc-b1fa-11f1-bd40-b312af735817</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 18:24:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>The 28th state? Carney's Canada draws closer to European Union</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260916-the-28th-state-carney-s-canada-draws-closer-to-european-union</link><description>
With a US president who talks of making Canada the 51st state, its leader in Europe where it’s not quite the EU's 28th state on offer, but something the president of the European Commission is calling ‘associate membership’. We’ll ask what that means, how it differs from the close status afforded to the likes of Iceland, Norway, Switzerland and the UK which Carney’s also visiting ahead of his own Strasbourg speech Thursday before the European Parliament. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3d723f5c-b1e2-11f1-88cf-757719c1152f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T083628Z-570247194-RC28KNAPX2ZW-RTRMADP-3-EU-PARLIAMENT-CARNEY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3d723f5c-b1e2-11f1-88cf-757719c1152f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T083628Z-570247194-RC28KNAPX2ZW-RTRMADP-3-EU-PARLIAMENT-CARNEY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b2e803d2-b1f8-11f1-9a1e-7d47b0bed310</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 18:19:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>arts24</category><title>Monica Bellucci in a Chilling French Home-Invasion Thriller</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260916-monica-bellucci-in-a-chilling-french-home-invasion-thriller</link><description>
On this week’s Arts 24, Manon Kerjean from Lost in Frenchlation joins Charlotte Lam to take a closer look at three French films of the moment: From a terrifying birthday party to a relationship that slowly turns toxic, this month’s French cinema brings plenty of tension, drama and dark humour.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e3c6c884-b1ef-11f1-bdb4-e5727ccb1647/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4911117226aaacac9c42e05-82662305.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e3c6c884-b1ef-11f1-bdb4-e5727ccb1647/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4911117226aaacac9c42e05-82662305.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b87667ec-b1f0-11f1-8de4-7fa1cf966426</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 17:04:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Charlotte Lam</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russian drone strike on a passenger bus in Ukraine kills 5 people and wounds at least 7 others</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/video/20260916-russian-drone-strike-on-a-passenger-bus-in-ukraine-kills-5-people-and-wounds-at-least-7-others</link><description>
A Russian drone struck a passenger bus in southern Ukraine early Wednesday, killing five people and wounding at least seven. President Volodymyr Zelenskyy described the attack, the latest in a series of Russian strikes on civilian transportation, as an “atrocity.” France 24's Gulliver Cragg tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d03dd9ec-b1d6-11f1-964b-cfc9bd8e913f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-130824-131208-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d03dd9ec-b1d6-11f1-964b-cfc9bd8e913f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-130824-131208-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dabba688-b1d6-11f1-99a8-3ddb603de1c5</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 16:17:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ivorian footballer Malick Yalcouyé falsely accused of lying about his age</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260916-ivorian-footballer-malick-yalcouy%C3%A9-falsely-accused-of-lying-about-his-age</link><description>
During a Premier League match between Chelsea and Brighton, social media users started spreading rumours that 20-year-old Ivorian footballer Malick Yalcouyé is older than he claims to be. The rumours gained such proportion that the youth club where he trained decided to post photos of Yalcouyé throughout the years. Recently, similar accusations were made against the new Real Madrid striker Yan Diomandé.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/faf0d2e8-a600-11f1-8e82-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Mod%C3%A8le-1920-x-1080-17.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/faf0d2e8-a600-11f1-8e82-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Mod%C3%A8le-1920-x-1080-17.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">43292096-b1ce-11f1-a567-2521ed09eebd</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 16:03:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/faf0d2e8-a600-11f1-8e82-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Mod%C3%A8le-1920-x-1080-17.png">© Premier League</source><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump administration plans to send powerful bombs to Israel in $2.8 billion weapons sale</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/video/20260916-trump-administration-plans-to-send-powerful-bombs-to-israel-in-2-8-billion-weapons-sale</link><description>
The Trump administration is planning to deliver powerful 2,000-pound bombs to Israel as part of an upcoming arms deal, weapons that prompted such concerns about the possibility of mass casualties in Gaza that the Biden administration paused their delivery two years ago. France 24's Philip Turle tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5ba9b4a8-b1e4-11f1-bcd1-e5727ccb1647/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-170436-170957-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5ba9b4a8-b1e4-11f1-bcd1-e5727ccb1647/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-170436-170957-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">62371eb4-b1e4-11f1-a9d3-7ddf861b5867</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:45:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>EU: An unprecedented offer to Canada</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/video/20260916-eu-an-unprecedented-offer-to-canada</link><description>
European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen on Wednesday proposed making Canada the European Union's first associate member, a striking overture as U.S. President Donald Trump's threats drive Ottawa closer to Europe.

Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney spoke of a "unique alliance with the EU".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/83f9a874-b1e3-11f1-aa33-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-170150-170333-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/83f9a874-b1e3-11f1-aa33-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-170150-170333-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8d020862-b1e3-11f1-a6f7-7fe7a0941dfb</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:41:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russia-Africa ties: Moscow's growing influence in Africa</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/video/20260916-russia-africa-ties-moscow-s-growing-influence-in-africa</link><description>
The third Russia-Africa Summit is due to bring African leaders to Moscow at the end of October, as ties between Russia and the continent continue to grow. The Kremlin has sought to expand its influence in Africa amid its isolation from the US and Europe, while African governments have pursued closer economic, diplomatic and security ties with Moscow.

Russia has also sought to draw African recruits into its war in Ukraine. Four years after the invasion, Kyiv estimates that around 3,000 Africans have ended up fighting for Moscow on the front lines. We discuss Russia's growing ties with Africa and the recruitment of African fighters with journalist Noé Michalon.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8a891d3c-b1de-11f1-aa4d-0dbbad64a63b/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260915-214547-215400-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8a891d3c-b1de-11f1-aa4d-0dbbad64a63b/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260915-214547-215400-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8fdd3c96-b1de-11f1-ab59-29821d8dc0ad</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:37:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Kenya: First World Athletics Championships to be held in Africa</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/video/20260916-kenya-first-world-athletics-championships-to-be-held-in-africa</link><description>
For the first time, the World Athletics Championships will be held on the African continent, with Kenya set to host the event in 2029.

World Athletics President Sebastian Coe described Kenya's bid as "convincing and moving".

Our Nairobi correspondent Bastien Renouil has the details.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/64057e76-b1de-11f1-bcd1-0dbbad64a63b/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260915-215612-215828-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/64057e76-b1de-11f1-bcd1-0dbbad64a63b/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260915-215612-215828-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">69913f6a-b1de-11f1-90ad-a1996acd38c0</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:36:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>DR Congo: Protests against plan to change the constitution</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/video/20260916-dr-congo-protests-against-plan-to-change-the-constitution</link><description>
In DR Congo, the C64 opposition coalition took to the streets of Kinshasa as the country's parliament returned for a new session. Its members have been opposing a proposed constitutional change backed by the ruling majority for several months.

Report by Aurélie Bazzara-Kibangula.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/254cbe2e-b1de-11f1-816d-e5727ccb1647/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260915-215412-215611-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/254cbe2e-b1de-11f1-816d-e5727ccb1647/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260915-215412-215611-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2b6fd1f6-b1de-11f1-b512-1d3251ddc0c2</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:31:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France in focus</category><title>Marie-Antoinette: France’s last queen and first influencer?</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/france-in-focus/20260916-marie-antoinette-france-s-last-queen-and-first-influencer</link><description>
This year, several French landmarks are paying tribute to France’s last queen, Marie-Antoinette. Despite her public execution taking place more than 230 years ago, the monarch continues to fascinate both at home and abroad. Our reporters dive into the reasons behind the lasting interest and explore why she could be considered France’s first influencer.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/19e155c2-b1cf-11f1-9543-e59e88953996/w:1024/p:16x9/marie-antoinette.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/19e155c2-b1cf-11f1-9543-e59e88953996/w:1024/p:16x9/marie-antoinette.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fcc0ce74-b1dc-11f1-80f8-ad599027b17e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:29:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Joanna COCKERELL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>WHO sees 'encouraging signs' in DR Congo Ebola response but says outbreak 'far from over'</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260916-who-sees-encouraging-signs-in-dr-congo-ebola-response-but-says-outbreak-far-from-over</link><description>
The World Health Organization said Wednesday that the fight against the Ebola outbreak in DR Congo was showing “encouraging signs" but that the epidemic was "far from over". More than 7,000 cases have been reported across seven provinces as of September 11.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0fff06cc-b1e2-11f1-93b2-e5727ccb1647/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T144444Z-226795097-RC2EGNAD8RRF-RTRMADP-3-HEALTH-EBOLA-WHO.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0fff06cc-b1e2-11f1-93b2-e5727ccb1647/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T144444Z-226795097-RC2EGNAD8RRF-RTRMADP-3-HEALTH-EBOLA-WHO.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c05d70b4-b1e0-11f1-bf01-f73169dd863e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:29:37 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0fff06cc-b1e2-11f1-93b2-e5727ccb1647/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T144444Z-226795097-RC2EGNAD8RRF-RTRMADP-3-HEALTH-EBOLA-WHO.jpg">© Gradel Muyisa Mumbere, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>In conversation with artist Nora Chipaumire</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/in-conversation-with-artist-nora-chipaumire-1</link><description>
Between dance, installation work, music making and more, artist Nora Chipaumire brings her ideas to Paris, hosted by the Résidence Tallard. Chipaumire is also leading performances and workshops at the Festival d'Automne, a contemporary arts festival in the French capital. At the heart of her work, she tells FRANCE 24, is a will to "shift the world into a much more positive, joyful" and equitable place. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ad642d14-b112-11f1-804d-4b311213e79e/w:1024/p:16x9/ANGL260915-0940-Live-CS0940-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ad642d14-b112-11f1-804d-4b311213e79e/w:1024/p:16x9/ANGL260915-0940-Live-CS0940-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">288f7778-b113-11f1-898b-d75620cbfd57</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:19:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Carys GARLAND</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Sanders, Bannon warn of AI dangers in rare US left-right alignment</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/video/20260916-sanders-bannon-warn-of-ai-dangers-in-rare-us-left-right-alignment</link><description>
Left-wing US Senator Bernie Sanders and Steve Bannon, a former adviser to President Donald Trump, warned against the dangers of artificial intelligence and its promoters on Tuesday, a sign that growing AI concern is scrambling political lines. we discuss that with our guest Bernard Benhamou, secretary general, Institute of digital soreignty.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3377562c-b1dd-11f1-91dd-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-161417-162350-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3377562c-b1dd-11f1-91dd-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-161417-162350-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3931e6e0-b1dd-11f1-8904-ad599027b17e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:19:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Alarm over AI grows as divided US Congress struggles to act</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/video/20260916-alarm-over-ai-grows-as-divided-us-congress-struggles-to-act</link><description>
The US Congress returned from recess Monday facing urgent warnings that artificial intelligence could spin dangerously out of control -- and little agreement over whether, or how, Washington should intervene.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/51f27ff6-b1dc-11f1-a6f7-3df65e1cd14d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-161209-161415-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/51f27ff6-b1dc-11f1-a6f7-3df65e1cd14d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-161209-161415-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">57471412-b1dc-11f1-8763-554674fe675d</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:18:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>EU opens door for Canada to become first 'associate member'</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/video/20260916-eu-opens-door-for-canada-to-become-first-associate-member</link><description>
European Commission President Ursula von ⁠der Leyen said ​on Wednesday she wanted to open the door for Canada to become the European Union's first "associate member". France 24's Douglas Herbert tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d120d508-b1db-11f1-aa36-3df65e1cd14d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-160115-160859-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d120d508-b1db-11f1-aa36-3df65e1cd14d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-160115-160859-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d9e66fe0-b1db-11f1-88d9-5b07398820e5</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:13:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Brazil's Supreme Court clashes over handling of probe involving judge</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/video/20260916-brazil-s-supreme-court-clashes-over-handling-of-probe-involving-judge</link><description>
Brazil's Supreme Court engaged in a heated, hours-long debate Tuesday over how to handle a potential probe into one of its top judges, in an unprecedented public showdown that has eclipsed a presidential election campaign.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d5627da4-b1d8-11f1-80e4-3ff9dda05487/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-141230-141423-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d5627da4-b1d8-11f1-80e4-3ff9dda05487/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-141230-141423-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dae0d118-b1d8-11f1-bfce-3bc722a8e87c</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:11:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French ex-minister Dati goes on trial in Renault-Nissan corruption case</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/video/20260916-french-ex-minister-dati-goes-on-trial-in-renault-nissan-corruption-case</link><description>
France's ex-culture minister Rachida Dati appeared in court Wednesday on corruption charges linked to dealings with the Renault-Nissan group, just months after her bruising defeat in the Paris mayoral race.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0b794ea4-b1d9-11f1-892b-f72ea3a769d9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-141424-141853-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0b794ea4-b1d9-11f1-892b-f72ea3a769d9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-141424-141853-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1187cf00-b1d9-11f1-977d-3f1d292844c3</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:09:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Kennedy Center will close for renovations after judge blocks returning Trump's name to building</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/video/20260916-kennedy-center-will-close-for-renovations-after-judge-blocks-returning-trump-s-name-to-building</link><description>
The Trump-aligned Kennedy Center board voted Tuesday to close most of the iconic performing arts venue just hours after a federal judge blocked the institution from returning President Donald Trump's name to the building.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cdec93d0-b1d7-11f1-9eb0-3ff9dda05487/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-141040-141213-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cdec93d0-b1d7-11f1-9eb0-3ff9dda05487/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-141040-141213-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d3de263c-b1d7-11f1-bfbe-61eb6dc2223d</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:07:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Countries move to ban social media for children</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/video/20260916-countries-move-to-ban-social-media-for-children</link><description>
The European Union unveiled proposals on Wednesday to ban social media for children under 13, as a growing number of countries look to restrict children's access to the platforms following a global backlash.
